From 04f98d4b9382a0d5177c0e5686816ca340527eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Formal gate: observe the exact release and clean locked
 dependencies at both ends

execute() now records one observation before the first Lean execution and one
after the last: the exact Lean release (4.34.1, commit 5045d005, Release), the
nine dependency HEADs equal to the lock with clean worktrees, and the bound
manifest digest. The two must be equal. Dependency cleanliness was never
checked before, and dependency HEADs were read only at the end. The receipt adds
workflow_run_attempt, dependency_worktrees and both observations; every
existing key is unchanged.

New RuntimeGuardTests controls fail on the previous gate: a dirty dependency
before or after execution, a wrong dependency at preflight (refused before the
old build is deleted), a well-formed runtime change between the observations,
and the receipt's attempt and observation fields.

Rotations: formal/manifest.json binds the new gate.py and test hashes, and the
five gate-hash literals in formal/tests move together (as in Math-#412).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cz7WZybv8znP64SpPj6sWY
